From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] winepipewire.drv: Report endpoint hotplug to mmdevapi.

GE's mmdevapi (JS Deck's hotplug support from xzn/proton-ds5-haptic,
reworked for the DualSense patches) asks the driver for endpoint deltas
from an update thread, which winepulse.drv answers. Implement the same
protocol here, so devices plugged in while a game runs show up and
IMMNotificationClient callbacks fire.

A registry listener on the main loop flags Audio/Sink and Audio/Source
node changes (a sink also wakes capture, for its monitor endpoint). The
delta call waits up to a second like winepulse, lets a burst of node
changes settle for 200 ms, takes a fresh probe and diffs it against the
endpoints mmdevapi has: added entries first, then removed ones, and
more_data when the other flow has pending changes. Endpoints that
survive keep their index and container id; their format and name are
refreshed. The default endpoints are never removed.

The probe in test_connect is split out so the refresh can reuse it.
WINEPIPEWIRE_HOTPLUG=0 turns the watcher off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
